{
  "$comment": [
    "Proposed Vietnamese patterns for src/data/claims-lint.json (patterns.vi of each rule) and src/data/keyword-map.json (seOwned.vi appended to the existing two, seOwnedLead.vi and reserved.G1.vi new). Not merged: the owner decides (M3 vi translator, 2026-10-06; QA record vi-qa.md, appendix A).",
    "Coverage: every claims-lint rule with per-locale patterns and no vi key yet — 26 rules. Skipped: jargon (already has vi), io-home and engine-claim ('*' only). hype keeps its '*' patterns and gets vi ones as well.",
    "Vietnamese writes every syllable as a separate word and most letters are outside ASCII: word edges are (?<![\\p{L}]) / (?![\\p{L}]), syllables inside a term are joined with \\s+, and no pattern relies on \\w or \\b (so the Unicode widening of bb689eb changes nothing). Matched case-insensitively with the u flag on the rendered text (placeholders filled, markup stripped), each rule keeping its own exempt / only key paths.",
    "Tested on HEAD 3d520ab + the vi copy: 0 hits on src/locales/vi.json; every counter-example in vi-qa.md appendix A hits its rule; the R39 / R83 words that must pass do not hit. Merged into a copy: build and --pseudo 0 errors, vi L-14 / L-9 warnings gone, check.mjs 0 / 0, tests 62/62."
  ],
